# Vue Component Rules

## shadcn-vue

- UI primitives live in `app/components/ui/` and are managed by CLI (`npx shadcn-vue@latest add`). Do not edit them manually.
- Use `cn()` from `~/lib/utils` to merge Tailwind classes conditionally.
- Import shadcn-vue components without path prefix (Nuxt auto-import).

## Styling

- Use Tailwind utility classes. Reference theme tokens via CSS variables (e.g. `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`).
- Do not use scoped `<style>` blocks for layout — use Tailwind.
- `<style scoped>` is acceptable only for component-specific animations or overrides that Tailwind cannot express.

## Structure

- Components are Nuxt auto-imported. Do not add explicit import statements for sibling components.
- Keep components focused on rendering. Extract shared state into `app/composables/`.
- Do not import from `app/notes/`, `app/storage/`, or `app/config/` directly — access domain data through composables.
